// A stand-in for Metal's standard library, so that a .metal file compiles as C++ on Linux and runs on
// the CPU (tools/metal/metal.py rewrites the source a little first; README.md says what it covers).
// The vector types are clang's extended vectors, the same machinery Metal's own compiler is built on:
// swizzles, splats and arithmetic behave as they do on the GPU. Only what Terra's shaders use, and its
// near relatives, is here: a shader that needs more adds it here, in the same change.
